endobj

333 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 288 0 R/E(My name is Vicent Manila, and over the past twelve months, I\220ve had the profound honour of serving as the President of AIESEC in Tanzania. This term has been more than just a leadership journey; it has been a milestone. Together with my team and local chapters across the country, we embarked on a mission to ascend to rise beyond limitations, build intentional impact, and shape a sustainable AIESEC.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[4]>>
endobj

334 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 288 0 R/E(What made this year even more significant is that it marked the 25th Anniversary of AIESEC in Tanzania. A quarter-century since young Tanzanians joined a global movement to develop leadership for peace and fulfilment of humankind\220s potential. Standing at this historic crossroads, we honoured the past, acknowledged the present, and dared to shape the future.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[5]>>
endobj

335 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 288 0 R/E(Throughout this term, we embraced the responsibility of legacy. We reimagined our national strategies, reinforced collaboration within East Africa, deepened our engagements with partners, and prioritised the growth of our people. We didn\220t just run programs, we built relevance. We didn\220t just measure performance, we nurtured purpose.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[6]>>
endobj

336 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 288 0 R/E(This year was about choosing to rise. To rise in how we serve our communities. To rise in how we empower our members. To rise in how we deliver value to our partners. From national forums to career fairs, from partner roundtables to local chapter development, this was a year where AIESEC in Tanzania walked in its values and rose with vision.As we celebrate 25 years of developing young leaders in Tanzania, may this report serve as a reflection of our collective ascent, one built on courage, belief, and unwavering commitment to youth leadership.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[7]>>
endobj

337 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 288 0 R/E(To all who have walked this journey with us, thank you for believing.)/Pg 12 0 R/K[8]>>
endobj

338 0 obj
<</Type/StructElem/S/P/P 288 0 R/E(With pride and gratitude,)/Pg 12 0 R/K[9]>>
